From 15265c292e3ead7ec7e9b1e6bad22037f80b727f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:24:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 159/159] OdfFile writer: an XLSX pivot table becomes a data
 pilot table

The converter wrote a pivot table as table:data-pilot-table with its
name and nothing else, no target range, source or fields, which the
schema rejects and LibreOffice cannot use: 37 of LibreOffice's ODF test
documents after the ninth batch. It now writes the target range from
the pivot's location, the source range from its cache, and its fields:
page fields, row and column fields (with the data layout field where
Excel has field -2), data fields with their function, and the cache's
other fields as hidden. A page field's selection is not carried yet:
it shows every page. A pivot table without a target or a field is not
written. x2t's reader already turns a data pilot table into an XLSX
pivot table, so the pivot table now survives the round trip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
